      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T10:41:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we do this, then every time an all calls setDelegateUid we might end up with a new receiver and a new death recipient. And the app would have no way of clearing death recipients it previously passed in. So we will have more and more death recipients. We probably want to store a binder object in the client-side CaptivePortal class.\n\nMaybe we could add something like this to CaptivePortal.java:\n\n    // Callback object that ConnectivityService can store and use to register\n    // death recipients. Initialized the first time that setDelegateUid() is called\n    // and never changed.\n    private final AtomicReference\u003cIBinder\u003e mCallbackBinder;\n\nand in setDelegateUid:\n\n    mCallbackBinder \u003d compareAndSet(null, new Binder());\n\nthen you would pass this binder to the setDelegateUid together with the UID and the result receiver. Then you could store this binder in the CaptivePortalImpl class using a similar AtomicReference. It would start off null, and the first time you change it from non-null to null (check the return value of compareAndSet) you could call linkToDeath. That ensure that as soon as setDelegateUid is called, the death recipient is registered, and no more death recipients are registered for this CaptivePortalImpl object in the future.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6390,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 6390,
        "endChar": 24
