      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T10:41:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "RemoteException means that netd is dead and the system will be crashing immediately. You might need to catch ServiceSpecificException, but hopefully not, since ConnectivityService and netd state should be in sync: networkAllowBypassVpnOnNetwork can throw ServiceSpecificExceptions with ENOENT or EEXIST, but I don\u0027t think that can ever happen if this code is correct.\n\nThat said, see above: if we use an OutcomeReceiver\u003cVoid, ServiceSpecificException\u003e, then maybe we can just pass that back to the caller. In some cases we might have to throw SSE locally, such as if the caller passes in -1 and there is nothing already in the map, we could throw new ServiceSpecificException(ENOENT).",
      "range": {
